  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Access to Healthcare for Refugees and People Displaced from Ukraine Benefitting of Temporary Protection in Member States</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">After one year of activation of the Temporary Protection Directive, the displaced population of Ukraine in the European Union still face challenges in accessing the national health system, including, language barriers, and lack of information and knowledge about available services. These barriers can result in refugees not receiving the care they need, leading to poor health outcomes and increased morbidity and mortality. The outcomes of the action are to a) increase capacities of health systems to cope with a displaced population; b) contribute to fight health inequalities in the Union, increasing the care for vulnerable populations; c) contribute to the health security in the Union guaranteeing that everybody has access to the necessary healthcare and prevention and treatment of diseases, including infectious diseases.The action therefore involves several activities that will be conducted by IOM:a) working with authorities responsible for health to adjust the health coverage to meet the needs of refugees and displaced persons benefitting of temporary protection.b) providing health mediators to ensure smooth access to healthcare for refugees, that don&#x2019;t know the system of the receiving countries.c) coordination of integrated services to maintain and improve the health status of displaced persons (such as co-operation of the health systems with NGOs and social workers, other governmental authorities, deployment of health teams to reach the refugee population, expanding assignment of health professionals to assess health needs of refugees and navigate them in the health systems)d) establishment of networks of health professionals working with refugees to facilitate the access and encouraging the use of the regular health services of the Member States by the displaced persons and supporting those professionals including via continuous education. e) establishment of health promotion programmes adapted to the reality of the displaced persons.The action aims to facilitate collaboration between stakeholders, including healthcare providers, government agencies, and refugee advocacy groups, to ensure that Ukrainian refugees have access to the healthcare services they need.</narrative>
  </description>
